{
  "title": "46: al-Ahqaaf الأحقاف",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nحٰمٓ‏(1)\nHAA-MEEM.\nHa Mim (H. M.)\nتَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ مِنَ اللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَكِيْمِ‏(2)\nTANZEELU KETAABE MENAL LAAHE A’ZEEZIL HAKEEM.\nThe descent (of the revelation) of this Book (Qur'an) (is) from God, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise\nمَا خَلَقْنَا السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَاۤ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ وَاَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى‌ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا عَمَّاۤ اُنْذِرُوْا مُعْرِضُوْنَ‏(3)\nMAA KHALAQNAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA ILLAA BIL-HAQQE WA AJALIM MOSAMMAA WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO A’MMAA AUNZEROOA MUA’REZOONA.\nWe created not the heavens and the earth and what is between them two, save with truth and (for) a determined term; But those who disbelieve turn away from what they are warned of\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ مَّا تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَرُوْنِىْ مَاذَا خَلَقُوْا مِنَ الْاَرْضِ اَمْ لَهُمْ شِرْكٌ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ‌ؕ اِیْتُوْنِىْ بِكِتٰبٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِ هٰذَاۤ اَوْ اَثٰرَةٍ مِّنْ عِلْمٍ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(4)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM MAA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE AAROONEAA MAA KHALAQOOA MENAL ARZE AM LAHUM SHERKUN FIL AS-SAMAAWAATE AETOONEAA BEKETAABIM MIN QABLE HAAZAA AW AASAARATIN MIN I’LMIN IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “Have ye seen what ye called upon besides God? Show me what of the earth did they create; or for them is there any share in the heavens? Bring me a book ere this or traces of knowledge, if ye be truthful.\nوَمَنْ اَضَلُّ مِمَّنْ يَّدْعُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَنْ لَّا يَسْتَجِيْبُ لَهٗۤ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ وَهُمْ عَنْ دُعَآئِهِمْ غٰفِلُوْنَ‏(5)\nWA MAN AZALLO MIMMAN YYADU’OOA MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAN LAA YASTAJEEBU LAHU ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE WA HUM A’N DUA’AAEHEM GHAAFELOON.\nAnd who is more astray than he who calleth upon besides God, unto such who will respond not unto him till the Day of Judgment, and they, of their invocations are not conscious\nوَاِذَا حُشِرَ النَّاسُ كَانُوْا لَهُمْ اَعْدَآءً وَّ كَانُوْا بِعِبَادَتِهِمْ كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(6)\nWA EZAA HUSHERA NAASO KAANOO LAHUM AAA’DAAAN WA KAANOO BEE’EBAADATEHEM KAAFEREEN.\nAnd when people shall be gathered together (on the Day of Reckoning) they shall be hostile unto them, and shall be the deniers of their worship (unto them)\nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِلْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْۙ هٰذَا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌؕ‏(7)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA BAYYENAAT QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAA-AHUM HAAZAA SEHRUM MMUBEENUN.\nAnd when Our clear signs are recited unto them, say those who disbelieve about the truth when it cometh unto them, this is an open sorcery\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ‌ؕ قُلْ اِنِ افْتَرَيْتُهٗ فَلَا تَمْلِكُوْنَ لِىْ مِنَ اللّٰهِ شَيئًا‌ ؕ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا تُفِيْضُوْنَ فِيْهِ‌ؕ كَفٰى بِهٖ شَهِيْدًاۢ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْ‌ ؕ وَهُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(8)\nAM YAQOOLOONA AFTARAAHU QUL ENIS AFTARAYTUH FALAA TAMLEKOONA LEE MENAL LAAHE SHAYAN HOWA A-A’LAMO BEMAA TUFEEZOONA FEEH KAFAA BEHI SHAHEEDAA BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM WA HOWA GHAFOORUL RAHEEM.\nOr they do say: “He hath forged it?” Say thou (then O' Our Apostle Muhammad!): “If I have forged it, then ye have not aught for me against (the wrath of) God. He knoweth best what (all) ye utter (in mocking) about it; Sufficeth He a witness between me and you; and He is the Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful\nقُلْ مَا كُنْتُ بِدْعًا مِّنَ الرُّسُلِ وَمَاۤ اَدْرِىْ مَا يُفْعَلُ بِىْ وَلَا بِكُمْؕ اِنْ اَتَّبِعُ اِلَّا مَا يُوْحٰٓى اِلَىَّ وَمَاۤ اَنَا اِلَّا نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(9)\nQUL MAA KUNTO BEDA’AN MENAL AR-RUSULE WA MAA AADREAA MAA YUFA’ALU BEE WA LAA BEKUM IN AATTABEU’U ILLAA MAA YOOHAA ELAYYA WA MAA ANAA ILLAA NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “I am not the first of the apostles (from God), I know not what will be done unto me, nor (what will be done) unto you; I follow not anything save what hath been revealed unto me, and I am not but an open warner.\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ كَانَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ وَكَفَرْتُمْ بِهٖ وَشَهِدَ شَاهِدٌ مِّنْۢ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ عَلٰى مِثْلِهٖ فَاٰمَنَ وَاسْتَكْبَرْتُمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(10)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN KAANA MIN I’NDIL LAAHE WA KAFARTUM BEHI WA SHAHEDA SHAAHEDUN MIN BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ A’LAA MESLEH FA-AAMANA WA TAKBARTUM INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nSay thou: “See ye? If (this Qur'an) be from God and ye disbelieve in it, (although) hath borne witness a witness from among the children of Israel, on its similarity (with the previous scriptures), and hath (also him-self) believed (in it), and yet ye in pride exalt yourselves; Verily God guideth not the unjust people.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَوْ كَانَ خَيْرًا مَّا سَبَقُوْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ‌ ؕ وَاِذْ لَمْ يَهْتَدُوْا بِهٖ فَسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ هٰذَاۤ اِفْكٌ قَدِيْمٌ‏(11)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LILLAZEENA AAMANOO LAW KAANA KHAYRAN MAA SABAQOONAA ELAYHE WA IZ LAM YAHTADOOA BEHI FASAYAQOOLOONA HAAZAA AEFKUN QADEEMUN.\nAnd say those who disbelieve about those who believe; “Had it been good, they would have gone not ahead of us unto it: “Since they seek not to be guided aright by it; say they: “This is a lie of old:\nوَمِنْ قَبْلِهٖ كِتٰبُ مُوْسٰٓى اِمَامًا وَّرَحْمَةً  ‌ ؕ وَهٰذَا كِتٰبٌ مُّصَدِّقٌ لِّسَانًا عَرَبِيًّا لِّيُنْذِرَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ‌ۖ  وَبُشْرٰى لِلْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(12)\nWA MIN QABLEHI KETAABU MOOSAA AEMAAMAN WA RAHMATAL WA KETAABUM MMUSADDEQUN LLESAANAN A’RABIYYAL LEYUNZERA LAZEENA ZALAMOO WABUSHRAA LIL-MUHSENEENA.\nAnd before it the Book of Moses (the Pentateuch ) was a guide and a mercy: and this (Qur'an) is a Book confirmeth (the previous scriptures), in the Arabic language that it may warn those who are unjust; and (contains) glad-tidings for the doers of good\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْا رَبُّنَا اللّٰهُ ثُمَّ اسْتَقَامُوْا فَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(13)\nINNAL LAZEENA QAALOO RABBONAA LAAHO SUMMA TATANAZZALO FALAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM HUM YAHZANOON.\nVerily, those who say: “Our Lord is God,” and are firm aright, then no fear shall be on them nor shall they grieve;\nاُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ ۚ جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(14)\nOOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN JANNAH KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA JA-ZAAA-AWN BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThese shall be inmates of the garden, abiding in it; a recompense for what they did\nوَوَصَّيْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ بِوَالِدَيْهِ اِحْسَانًا‌ ؕ حَمَلَتْهُ اُمُّهٗ كُرْهًا وَّوَضَعَتْهُ كُرْهًا‌ ؕ وَحَمْلُهٗ وَفِصٰلُهٗ ثَلٰثُوْنَ شَهْرًا‌ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا بَلَغَ اَشُدَّهٗ وَبَلَغَ اَرْبَعِيْنَ سَنَةً  ۙ قَالَ رَبِّ اَوْزِعْنِىْۤ اَنْ اَشْكُرَ نِعْمَتَكَ الَّتِىْۤ اَنْعَمْتَ عَلَىَّ وَعَلٰى وَالِدَىَّ وَاَنْ اَعْمَلَ صَالِحًا تَرْضٰٮهُ وَاَصْلِحْ لِىْ فِىْ ذُرِّيَّتِىْ ؕۚ اِنِّىْ تُبْتُ اِلَيْكَ وَاِنِّىْ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(15)\nWA INSAANA INSAANA EHSAANANW HAMALATHU AUMMUH KURHAN WWAWAZAA’ATHU KURHAN WAHAMLUH WAFESAALUH SALAASOONA SHAHRAN HATTAA EZAA BALAGHA ASHUDDAHU WA BALAGHA ARBA-E’ENA SANATAN QAALA RABBE AWZE’NEE AN ASHKORA NE’MATAKAL LATEE ANA’MTA A’LAYYA WA A’LAA WAALEDAYYA WA A-A’MALA SAALEHAN TARZAAHO WAASLEH LEE FEE ZURREETEAA INNEE TUBTU ELAYKA WA INNEE MENAL AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\nAnd We have enjoined on man goodness unto his parents; Did bear him his mother with pain and she delivered him with pain; And bearing him and weaning him is thirty months; Until when he attaineth his maturity and reacheth forty years, sayeth he: “My Lord! arouse me that I may give thanks for Thy bounties which Thou hath bestowed on me and my parents and that I may do good which pleaseth Thee and do good unto me in respect of my offspring; Verily I turn unto Thee (repentant)., and verily I am one of the Muslims\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ نَتَقَبَّلُ عَنْهُمْ اَحْسَنَ مَا عَمِلُوْا وَنَتَجَاوَزُ عَنْ سَيِّاٰتِهِمْ فِىْۤ اَصْحٰبِ الْجَنَّةِ‌ ؕ وَعْدَ الصِّدْقِ الَّذِىْ كَانُوْا يُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(16)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA NATAQABBALU A’NHUM AHSANAL MAA A’MELOO WANATAJAAWAZU A’N SAYYEAATEHIM FEE ASHAABIL JANNAH WA’DAL AS-SEDQE LAZEE KAANOO YOOA’ADOONA.\nThese are they from whom We accept the best of what they have done and pass by their evils, (they shall be) among the inmates of the Garden; (this is that) promise of truth which they were used to be promised.\nوَالَّذِىْ قَالَ لِوَالِدَيْهِ اُفٍّ لَّكُمَاۤ اَتَعِدٰنِنِىْۤ اَنْ اُخْرَجَ وَقَدْ خَلَتِ الْقُرُوْنُ مِنْ قَبْلِىْ‌ ۚ وَهُمَا يَسْتَغِيْثٰنِ اللّٰهَ وَيْلَكَ اٰمِنْ ۖ  اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ  ۖۚ فَيَقُوْلُ مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(17)\nWAL LAZEE QAALA LEWAALEDAYHE AUFFIN LLAKUMAA AATAE’EDAANENEAA AN AUKHRAJA WA QAD KHALATE AL-QUROONU MIN QABLEAA WAHUMAA YASTAGHEESAANE LAAHA WAYLAKA AAAMEN INNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN FAYAQOOLO MAA HAAZAA ILLAA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nAnd he who sayeth unto his parents: “Fie on ye both! Promise ye me that I shall be brought forth (from the grave alive) when have passed away generations before me?” and they both implore for God’s aid, (saying): “Woe unto thee! Believe thou; for verily the promise of God is true;” Then will he say: “This is naught but stories of the ancients.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ حَقَّ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقَوْلُ فِىْۤ اُمَمٍ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا خٰسِرِيْنَ‏(18)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA HAQQA A’LAYHEMUL QAWLO FEE OMAMIN QAD KHALAT MIN QABLEHIM MENAL JINNE WAL AENSE INNAHUM KAANOO KHAASEREEN.\nThese are they against whom the sentence hath been proved among the peoples of the jinn and the men that have passed away before them; verily they were the losers.\nوَلِكُلٍّ دَرَجٰتٌ مِّمَّا عَمِلُوْا‌ ۚ وَلِيُوَفِّيَهُمْ اَعْمَالَهُمْ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(19)\nWA DARAJAATUN MIMMAA A’MELOO WALEEWAFFEEHUM A-A’MAALAHUM WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nAnd for all (are ranks) (assigned) according to what they did, and that He may (fully) recompense their deeds, and they shall not be done any injustice.\nوَيَوْمَ يُعْرَضُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا عَلَى النَّارِ ؕ اَذْهَبْتُمْ طَيِّبٰتِكُمْ فِىْ حَيَاتِكُمُ الدُّنْيَا وَاسْتَمْتَعْتُمْ بِهَا ‌ۚ فَالْيَوْمَ تُجْزَوْنَ عَذَابَ الْهُوْنِ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَبِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَفْسُقُوْنَ‏(20)\nWA YAWMA YUA’RAZU LAZEENA KAFAROO A’LAL NAAR AAZHABTUM TAYBAATEKUM FEE HAYAATEKUMU DUNYAA WAASTAMTAA’TUM BEHAA FALYAWMA TUJZAWNA A’ZAABAL HOONE BEMAA KUNTUM TASTAKBEROONA FIL ARZE BEGHAYRIL HAQQE WA BEMAA KUNTUM TAFSUQOONA.\nAnd on the day when shall be exposed those who dis-believed to the fire: (it will be said unto them): “Ye did away with your good things in your life of the world and ye took your fill of pleasure in them; This day therefore ye shall be recompensed with shameful chastisement for what ye used to act in arrogance in the earth without any right, and for what ye used to transgress.\nوَاذْكُرْ اَخَا عَادٍؕ اِذْ اَنْذَرَ قَوْمَهٗ بِالْاَحْقَافِ وَقَدْ خَلَتِ النُّذُرُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهٖۤ اَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(21)\nWAAZKUR AAKHAA A’AADIN IZ AANZARA QAWMAH BIL-AAHQAAFE WA QAD KHALATE AN-NUZURU MIN BAYNE YADAYHE WA MIN KHALFEH ALLAA TA’BODOO ILLAA LAAHA INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nAnd remember (O' Our Apostle Muhammad!) of the brother of ’Ad when he warned his people of ‘Al-Ahqaf’ and (while) indeed warners have been before him and after him (saying) “Worship ye not but God! Verily, I fear for you the chastisement of a grievous day.\nقَالُوْۤا اَجِئْتَنَا لِتَاْفِكَنَا عَنْ اٰلِهَتِنَا‌ ۚ فَاْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(22)\nQAALOO AAJETANAA LETAAFEKANAA A’N AAALEHATENAA FAATENAA BEMAA TAE’EDUNAA IN KUNTA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\nSaid they: “What! Come thou unto us to turn us away from our gods? Then bring thou on us what thou threateneth us with, if thou art of the truthful ones.\nقَالَ اِنَّمَا الْعِلْمُ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ‌ۖ وَاُبَلِّغُكُمْ مَّاۤ اُرْسِلْتُ بِهٖ وَلٰكِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮكُمْ قَوْمًا تَجْهَلُوْنَ‏(23)\nQAALA INNAMAA I’LMO I’NDAL LAAHE WAABALLEGHUKUM MAA AURSELTU BEHI WALAAKENNEAA AARAAKUM QAWMAN TAJHALOON.\nSaid he: “The knowledge (of it) is only with God, I only convey unto you the message which I am sent with, but I see you a people who are ignorant.\nفَلَمَّا رَاَوْهُ عَارِضًا مُّسْتَقْبِلَ اَوْدِيَتِهِمْ ۙ قَالُوْا هٰذَا عَارِضٌ مُّمْطِرُنَا‌ ؕ بَلْ هُوَ مَا اسْتَعْجَلْتُمْ بِهٖ ‌ۚ رِيْحٌ فِيْهَا عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌۙ‏(24)\nFALAMMAA RA-AW-HO A’AAREZAN MMUSTAQBELA AAWDEETEHEM QAALOO HAAZAA A’AAREZUN MMUMTERUNAA BAL HOWA MAA ASTAA’JALTUM BEHI REEHUN FEEHAA A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nSo when they saw (the punishment in the form of) a cloud advancing unto their valleys, they said: “This is a cloud which will give us rain;” Nay! it is (the calamity) what ye sought to hasten on; a blast of a violent wind in which is a painful chastisement,\nتُدَمِّرُ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ ۭ بِاَمْرِ رَبِّهَا فَاَصْبَحُوْا لَا يُرٰٓى اِلَّا مَسٰكِنُهُمْ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْقَوْمَ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(25)\nTUDAMMERU KULLA SHAY-IN BE-AMRE RABBEHAA FA-ASBAHOO LAA YURAAA ILLAA MASAAKENUHUM KAZAALEKA NAJZIL QAWMAZ MUJREMEEN.\nDestroying every thing by the command of its Lord; So became they not to be seen save their dwellings; Thus do We recompense the guilty people.\nوَلَقَدْ مَكَّنّٰهُمْ فِيْمَاۤ اِنْ مَّكَّنّٰكُمْ فِيْهِ وَجَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ سَمْعًا وَّاَبْصَارًا وَّاَفْئِدَةً  ۖ فَمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْهُمْ سَمْعُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَبْصَارُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَفْئِدَتُهُمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ اِذْ كَانُوْا يَجْحَدُوْنَۙ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(26)\nWA LAQAD MAKKANNAAHUM FEEMAA IN MMAKKANNAAKUM FEEHE WA JA-A’LNAA LAHUM SAMA’AN WWAABSAARAN WWAAFEDATAN FAMAA AGHNAA A’NHUM SAM-O’HUM WA LAA AABSAARUHUM WA LAA AAFEDATUHUM MIN SHAY-IN IZ KAANOO YAJHADOON BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WAHAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nAnd certainly had We firmly established them, what We established not ye in it, and We had given them ears, and eyes and hearts; but availed not them aught their ears nor their eyes nor their hearts, since they gainsaid the signs of God, and they were encircled by what they used to mock at.\nوَلَقَدْ اَهْلَكْنَا مَا حَوْلَكُمْ مِّنَ الْقُرٰى وَصَرَّفْنَا الْاٰيٰتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(27)\nWA LAQAD AHLAKNAL MAA HAWLAKUM MENAL KORAA WASARRAFNAA AAYAATE LA-A’LLAHUM YARJE-O’ON.\nAnd indeed We destroyed of the towns which are around you, and We did display Our signs that they might turn (unto Us).\nفَلَوْلَا نَصَرَهُمُ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ قُرْبَانًا اٰلِهَةً ؕ بَلْ ضَلُّوْا عَنْهُمْ‌ۚ وَذٰلِكَ اِفْكُهُمْ وَمَا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(28)\nFA-LAWLAA NASARAHUMU LAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONIL LAAHE QURBAANAN AALEHATAL BAL ZALLOOA A’NHUM ZAKAATA AEFKUHUM WA MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nWhy then did not help them those whom they took for gods besides God, in approaching nigh unto God? Nay! but they failed them, and this was their lie and what they used to forge.\nوَاِذْ صَرَفْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ نَفَرًا مِّنَ الْجِنِّ يَسْتَمِعُوْنَ الْقُرْاٰنَ‌ۚ فَلَمَّا حَضَرُوْهُ قَالُوْۤا اَنْصِتُوْا‌ۚ فَلَمَّا قُضِىَ وَلَّوْا اِلٰى قَوْمِهِمْ مُّنْذِرِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA IZ SARAFNAA ELAYKA NAFARAN MENAL JINNE YASTAMEU’OONA QURAANA FALAMMAA HAZAROOHU QAALOO AANSETOOA FALAMMAA QUZEAAA WALLAW ELAA QAWMEHIM MMUNZEREENA.\nAnd when turned We unto thee a party of jinn who (quietly) listened to the Qur’an when came they unto it, said they: “Be ye silent! (and listen)?” then when was finished (the recital), returned they unto their people warning (them against the wrath of God)\nقَالُوْا يٰقَوْمَنَاۤ اِنَّا سَمِعْنَا كِتٰبًا اُنْزِلَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مُوْسٰى مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ يَهْدِىْۤ اِلَى الْحَقِّ وَاِلٰى طَرِيْقٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(30)\nQAALOO YAAQAWMANAA INNAA SAMEA’NAA KETAABAA UNZELA MIN BA’DE MOOSAA MOSADDEQAL LEMAA BAYNA YADAYHE YAHDEE ELAL HAQQE WA ELAA TAREEQIN MUSTAQEEM.\nSaid (the Jinns): “O’ ye our people! Verily, have we listened unto a Book sent down (from God) after Moses, verifying what is before it, guiding unto the truth and unto a path straight aright.\nيٰقَوْمَنَاۤ اَجِيْبُوْا دَاعِىَ اللّٰهِ وَاٰمِنُوْا بِهٖ يَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ مِّنْ ذُنُوْبِكُمْ وَيُجِرْكُمْ مِّنْ عَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍ‏(31)\nYAAQAWMANAA AAJEEBOOA DAAE’EAAA LAAHE WA AAMENOO BEHI YAGHFER LAKUM MIN ZUNOOBEKUM WAYUJERKUM MIN A’ZAABIN A’ZAABAN LEEMIN.\nO’ ye our people! Respond ye (all) unto the Summoner unto God and believe ye in Him, He will forgive you of your sins, and guard you against a painful chastisement.\nوَمَنْ لَّا يُجِبْ دَاعِىَ اللّٰهِ فَلَيْسَ بِمُعْجِزٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَيْسَ لَهٗ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اَوْلِيَآءُ ‌ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(32)\nWA MAN LAA YUJEB DAAE’EAAA LAAHE FA-LAYSA BEMUA’JEZIN FIL ARZE BE-AN LAHU MIN DOONEHI ANNAKUM AWLEYAAA-O OOLAAA-EKA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nAnd whosoever respondeth not unto the Summoner unto God, yet he can frustrate not God’s will in the earth, and there shall not be for him, other than Him, any guardians; these are in manifest error\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَلَمْ يَعْىَ بِخَلْقِهِنَّ بِقٰدِرٍ عَلٰۤی اَنْ يُّحْیِۦَ الْمَوْتٰى ‌ؕ بَلٰٓى اِنَّهٗ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏‏(33)\nAWALAM YARAW ANNAL LAAHA LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA LAM YAA’AAA BEKHALQEHENA WAL-ARZA A’ALAA AN YUH MAWTAA BALAAA AENAH A’LAA KULE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nWhat! Have they not seen that God Who created the heavens and the earth and was not wearied by their creation, hath power to give life unto the dead? Aye! Verily, He is over all things powerful.\nوَيَوْمَ يُعْرَضُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا عَلَى النَّارِ ؕ اَلَيْسَ هٰذَا بِالْحَقِّ‌ ؕ قَالُوْا بَلٰى وَرَبِّنَا‌ ؕ قَالَ فَذُوْقُوا الْعَذَابَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(34)\nWA YAWMA YUA’RAZU LAZEENA KAFAROO A’LAL NAAR A-LAYSA HAAZAA BIL-HAQQE QAALOO BALAA WARABBENAA QAALA FAZOOQOOA A’ZAABA BEMAA KUNTUM TAKFOROONA.\nAnd on the day when shall be exposed those who disbelieved, to the fire (it will be asked of them): “Is this not the truth?” They shall say: “Aye! By our Lord!” then He will say: “Taste ye (now) the chastisement for what ye used to disbelieve\nفَاصْبِرْ كَمَا صَبَرَ اُولُوا الْعَزْمِ مِنَ الرُّسُلِ وَلَا تَسْتَعْجِلْ لَّهُمْ‌ؕ كَاَنَّهُمْ يَوْمَ يَرَوْن مَا يُوْعَدُوْنَۙ لَمْ يَلْبَثُوْۤا اِلَّا سَاعَةً مِّنْ نَّهَارٍ ‌ؕ بَلٰغٌ ۚ فَهَلْ يُهْلَكُ اِلَّا الْقَوْمُ الْفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(35)\nFAS-BIR KAMAA SABARA ULUL AL-A’AZME MENAL AR-RUSULE WA LAA TASTAA’JEL LAHUM KA-ANNAHUM YAWMA YARAWN MAA YOOA’ADOONA LAM YALBASOOA ILLAA SAAA’ATAN MIN NNAHAARIN BALAAGHUN FA HAL YUHLAKU ILLAA AL-QAWMU FAASEQOON.\nTherefore (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) bear thou up with patience, as did the apostles endowed with constancy and seek thou not to hasten for them (their doom); On the day when they will see what they have been promised, (it shall be unto them) as if they tarried not but (for only) an hour of the day; (a clear) Deliverance! (this is)! then shall be destroyed any but the transgressing people.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Ahqaaf (The Sandhills)\nThis is a ‘Makki’ Surah and it has 35 verses. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that a person who recites this Surah daily, or at least every Friday, will remain safe from all the dangers of this world and the hereafter.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of creatures that walk on this Earth and an equal number of sins will be forgiven. Keeping this Surah as a talisman acts as a protection and means of averting all kinds of difficulties.\nIf a person dissolved this Surah in zamzam water and then drinks it, he will be greatly honoured by the people and what he says will never be rejected. He will also remember everything he hears. It acts as a cure for disease and a protection from the Jinn."
